<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mongol Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mongol</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mongol Empire was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> in 1206 and became the largest contiguous land empire in history, stretching from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> to eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. Its conquests destroyed states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmian-empire">Khwarazmian Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>. In the later thirteenth century it divided into successor khanates, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mongol-empire.jpg" alt="Mongol Empire" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DannamEmpire · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Expansion_of_the_Mongol_Empire_1206%E2%80%931294.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>It was a territorial appanage (ulus) that Genghis Khan assigned to his second son Chagatai when he divided the <b>Mongol Empire</b>'s conquests, and this inherited subordination marked the khanate for much of its existence.</blockquote><a href="/empire/chagatai-empire">Chagatai Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Crimean Khanate was one of the successor states of the Golden Horde, the western part of the <b>Mongol Empire</b>, which broke apart in the fifteenth century into rival khanates.</blockquote><a href="/empire/crimean-khanate">Crimean Khanate · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Golden Horde grew out of the share of the <b>Mongol Empire</b> that Genghis Khan assigned to his eldest son Jochi: the western steppe beyond the Irtysh and whatever lands further west the Mongols might conquer.</blockquote><a href="/empire/golden-horde">Golden Horde · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Ilkhanate grew out of the westward expansion of the <b>Mongol Empire</b> under Hulagu Khan, a grandson of Genghis Khan.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Its rulers were tributaries in turn of the Abbasid Caliphate, the Seljuk Empire, the Kingdom of Georgia, the <b>Mongol Empire</b> and the Ilkhanate, and later of the Timurids and the Aq Qoyunlu, paying tribute and supplying troops while the dynasty endured at home.</blockquote><a href="/empire/shirvanshah-state">Shirvanshah State · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>The sultans became vassals, paying heavy tribute first to the <b>Mongol Empire</b> and then to the Ilkhanate.</blockquote><a href="/empire/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
